| **No security‑related middleware** (Helmet, CORS, rate‑limiter, etc.) | Leaves default Express headers (`X‑Powered‑By`) and no protection against common attacks. |
| **Public `/users` endpoint** returns a static list of user data | **A01 – Broken Access Control** – anyone can enumerate user details (even if static, it demonstrates the pattern). |
