### 2️⃣ Load Secrets from a **Secrets Manager** at runtime  

Below are three common, production‑grade patterns (AWS, GCP, HashiCorp Vault). Choose the one that matches your cloud provider.

#### A. AWS Secrets Manager (Node.js)

```js
// secrets.js – centralised secret loader
const { SecretsManagerClient, GetSecretValueCommand } = require('@aws-sdk/client-secrets-manager');

const client = new SecretsManagerClient({ region: process.env.AWS_REGION || 'us-east-1' });

/**
 * Retrieves a secret (JSON string) from AWS Secrets Manager.
 * The secret value is cached in memory for the life of the process.
 */
let secretCache = null;
async function getSecrets() {
  if (secretCache) return secretCache;

  const command = new GetSecretValueCommand({
    SecretId: process.env.AWS_SECRET_NAME || 'my-app/secrets', // name of the secret
  });

  const response = await client.send(command);
  const secretString = response.SecretString; // expects JSON
  secretCache = JSON.parse(secretString);
  return secretCache;
}

module.exports = { getSecrets };
```

**Usage in `app.js`**

```js
// At the top of app.js (after other imports)
const { getSecrets } = require('./secrets');

(async () => {
  const secrets = await getSecrets();          // <-- fetch once at startup
  const JWT_SECRET = secrets.JWT_SECRET;       // e.g. { "JWT_SECRET": "....", "STRIPE_SECRET": "..." }

  // make JWT secret available to the rest of the file
  // (or export it in a config object)
  // …rest of the server setup…
})();
```

*Benefits*  
* IAM‑based access – only the EC2/ECS task role that runs the container can read the secret.  
* Automatic rotation support (you can rotate in AWS and the app will pick up the new value on next restart).  
* Secrets are encrypted at rest and in‑transit.

#### B. Google Cloud Secret Manager (Node.js)

```js
// secrets-gcp.js
const { SecretManagerServiceClient } = require('@google-cloud/secret-manager');
const client = new SecretManagerServiceClient();

async function getSecret(secretName) {
  const [version] = await client.accessSecretVersion({ name: secretName });
  const payload = version.payload?.data?.toString();
  return JSON.parse(payload);
}

module.exports = { getSecret };
```

```js
